# DataGuard Windsurf Rules

- Read `AGENTS.md`, `rules/workspace_governance.md`, and the active plan before structural work.
- `src/` is production DataGuard source; validate changed contracts with the appropriate .NET build/test command.
- Keep product documentation and knowledge in their canonical directories; do not create root clutter or a parallel runtime/toolchain.
- Co-update documentation only when a verified observable contract changes; do not preserve stale product claims.
- Before irreversible cleanup, preserve WIP and obtain an owner-approved `from → keep | extract | rewrite | remove` manifest.
- Local agent state, caches, and handoffs are not documentation and are not disposable without the owning tool/session being stopped.

